## 8. Is this 2000? A checklist, not a story

| Feature | 2000 | Now | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Spending far ahead of revenue | Yes | Yes | Similar |
| Suppliers financing their customers | Yes | Reported, not fully verified | Similar if confirmed |
| Interest rates rising | Yes | Fed described as turning hawkish | Similar |
| Main buyers living on debt | Yes | Largest buyers are highly profitable | Different |
| Prices at extreme multiples of profit | Yes | Lower on current profit, but current profit may be a peak | Unclear |

The deciding variable is whether the self-funded buyers cut spending. One past episode is a sample of one, so use the checklist to form questions, not to predict the path.

## 9. Scenarios and signposts

| Scenario | What happens | Signposts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Correction | Capex holds; prices recover within months | Buyers raise or hold budgets; credit spreads narrow |
| Cyclical bust | Capex cut 30–40%; borrowers restructure; seller profits fall sharply, then recover in two to three years | A large buyer cuts guidance; supplier inventories build; a borrower fails to refinance |
| Structural bust | AI revenue does not arrive at scale; a multi-year decline | AI revenue growth stalls; write-downs of data-centre assets |

Assign your own probabilities and update them at each signpost.

